                    },
                    "message": "Please fix the traces (log -> lg2). The other comments are recommended, but not required."
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1297,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chris Cain",
                        "email": "cjcain@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "cjcain"
                    },
                    "message": "This is the old trace format and they have all been converted to using lg2 (due to efficiency and readability)\nChange all of them to lg2::debug(), lg2::error(), etc..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1297,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sheldon Bailey",
                        "email": "baileysh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baileysh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1312,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chris Cain",
                        "email": "cjcain@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "cjcain"
                    },
                    "message": "Instead of doing this conversion on the fly for every section, you could just read and use the value directly and assign constants to use in your check.\n\nconstexpr auto EXTN_LABEL_PWRM_MEMORY_POWER = \"5057524d\";\n\nif (labelValue == EXTN_LABEL_PWRM_MEMORY_POWER) ..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1312,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sheldon Bailey",
                        "email": "baileysh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baileysh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1325,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chris Cain",
                        "email": "cjcain@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "cjcain"
                    },
                    "message": "This file read will be done for every EXTN section, but only needed if it matches one of the two strings you want, so I would move it in the check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1325,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sheldon Bailey",
                        "email": "baileysh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baileysh"
                    },
                    "message": "Left out to allow other data to be done later if needed.\nagreed if this is the only data we wanted, then inside the check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1359,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chris Cain",
                        "email": "cjcain@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "cjcain"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you read the extnValue as an integer (in line 1325) instead of having to do string conversion here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "occ_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 1359,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sheldon Bailey",
                        "email": "baileysh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baileysh"
                    },
                    "message": "The file has hex characters in it, Last 4 hex characters are needed.\nspec byte 5 and 6 is the current (mem,proc) power, unlike other sensors \nthat read in one number.\nWhen I tried to read in as integer, then convert to hex to grab the last 4 digits was more work."
                },
                {
